From: SteamOS ARM port
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: sy7758: the enable GPIO is optional

On boards that keep the chip enabled in hardware the device tree has no
enable GPIO. The probe then fails with -ENOENT, the panel defers forever
waiting for its backlight, and with it the display, the GPU and the
DisplayPort sound card never come up. The driver does nothing with the
GPIO after probe, so carry on without one.

---
 drivers/video/backlight/sy7758.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/video/backlight/sy7758.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/sy7758.c
@@ -185,7 +185,7 @@ static int sy7758_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	fsleep(100);
 
 	/* Get enable GPIO and set to high */
-	sydev->gpio = devm_gpiod_get(dev, "enable", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
+	sydev->gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "enable", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
 	if (IS_ERR(sydev->gpio))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(sydev->gpio),
 				     "failed to get enable GPIO\n");
